KIconThemeDir: read each directory once instead of a stat per lookup

An icon missing from the current theme is searched for in every
directory of every inherited theme, one QFileInfo::exists() per
directory and extension: opening Plasma's launcher the first time costs
about 1,700 of them for the icons of a few applications and categories
(org.kde.dolphin alone 550). Where every file system call is slow
(under proot, which translates each one), that is most of the half
second before the launcher shows.

Each directory now keeps the hashes of its file names, read with one
opendir()/readdir() and again once they are older than ten seconds, so
icons installed later still show up. A name that is listed is still
checked with QFileInfo::exists(); themes in Qt resources are looked up
as before.

